The vendored htslib is built without its configure step, which is not
committed in the bundled htslib. This minimal config.h disables every
optional compression library: only zlib is available in WASM via the
emscripten port, so bz2/lzma/libdeflate are stripped. The native build uses
the same config.h, so both builds read the same files.

diff --git a/htslib/config.h b/htslib/config.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f3cd5eb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/htslib/config.h
@@ -0,0 +1,4 @@
+#ifndef _XOPEN_SOURCE
+#define _XOPEN_SOURCE 600
+#endif
+#define HAVE_DRAND48 1
